Method, data, and hosted service
--------------------------------

The "SemKNN" cost-aware routing method described in the accompanying paper
is the subject of ongoing research. The trained SemKNN artifacts and the
benchmark datasets they were produced from are NOT distributed with this
release. The public package contacts a small backend service to obtain
SemKNN recommendations; the backend never receives the user's prompt, only
a unit-norm embedding vector and a scalar lambda value. See the README
section on "Privacy & data flow" for the full description.

Users who would like to run the SemKNN router fully on-premise (for
regulated environments or air-gapped deployments) may license the backend
image and the trained artifacts under separate commercial terms; contact
the authors.


Anonymous usage telemetry
-------------------------

AgentCodec sends anonymous usage telemetry by default — but only when
you're using SemKNN routing. The payload covers technique chosen,
latency, predicted vs. observed quality, token counts, the prompt
embedding (already sent for SemKNN routing), and a canonical
model-family fingerprint. It does NOT include prompts, model outputs,
reference answers, concrete model names, API keys, or any user
identifier. A per-process ephemeral session_id is sent so server-side
analytics can group events from one module instance without correlating
across runs or users. Fixed / ACMTable / ACMLinear routes send no
telemetry at all.

To disable telemetry entirely:

    export AGENTCODEC_TELEMETRY=0

See the README section "Anonymous telemetry" for the full payload list,
the privacy invariants we test, and how to point telemetry at your own
collector instead of the default endpoint.


