Prior-method baselines: paper attribution + reference-implementation credit
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

The seven prior-method baselines shipped under ``agentcodec/techniques/
baselines.py`` (Self-Consistency, Self-Refine, Chain-of-Verification,
Best-of-N, Weighted Best-of-N, CISC, Mixture-of-Agents) are
re-implementations from the cited papers — no source code was copied
from any of the listed reference repositories. Each class docstring
carries the canonical paper citation with arXiv ID, author, and year.

Two of the baselines additionally reference an open-source reference
implementation in their docstrings as context; we did not copy code
from either:

  - CISC  — google-research/google-research/cisc (Apache License 2.0)
            Copyright 2025 Google LLC.
            Re-implemented from Taubenfeld et al. 2025 (arXiv:2502.06233).
            Source: https://github.com/google-research/google-research/tree/master/cisc

  - MoA   — togethercomputer/MoA (Apache License 2.0)
            Copyright 2024 Together Computer, Inc.
            Re-implemented from Wang et al. 2025 (arXiv:2406.04692).
            Source: https://github.com/togethercomputer/MoA

